p9w|v|To wander; to roam; to stray. ; To deviate from the true course; to miss the thing aimed at. ; To miss intellectual truth; to fall into error; to mistake in judgment or opinion; to be mistaken. ; To deviate morally from the right way; to go astray, in a figurative sense; to do wrong; to sin. ; To offend, as by erring.	d:2fi,45,7;1xx3,26,3~2fi,45,7;1xx3,26,3	D:22p7,25,4~22p7,25,4
